{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_e0bc7f42fde1e400631e8ccbd4af452b56b3082bc6269ef5a45363d645f48a89"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project targets Python 3.12 or later, installs via `uv sync --locked` plus `uv tool install --editable .`, and requirements.txt contains an editable self-dependency."}],"claim_ids":["clm_e0bc7f42fde1e400631e8ccbd4af452b56b3082bc6269ef5a45363d645f48a89"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_8be18b33b8654d1aac5cfc1bee291acb","id":"pg_09407ab2ecb8548793464ce58c86d565","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/elpsykongloo-paperbanana-pro-requirements-txt-3d9d1f11647e-4ce58c86d565.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_4d1662b6173a59ee98247d8b8c8b1d44"],"title":"elpsykongloo/PaperBanana-Pro/requirements.txt @ 3d9d1f11647e","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8be18b33b8654d1aac5cfc1bee291acb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_c3f187c26298c37cd29811b8009d101f660b3bfdfc58683e88e02b7084d909dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the project adopts a Contributor Covenant v1.4-based code of conduct and follows Google's Open Source Community Guidelines."}],"claim_ids":["clm_c3f187c26298c37cd29811b8009d101f660b3bfdfc58683e88e02b7084d909dc"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_8be18b33b8654d1aac5cfc1bee291acb","id":"pg_3430606e6f8e55718e7ed994f68124d3","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/elpsykongloo-paperbanana-pro-code-of-conduct-md-3d9d1f11647e-d994f68124d3.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_95d880446aec5942bed246d710084c8b"],"title":"elpsykongloo/PaperBanana-Pro/code-of-conduct.md @ 3d9d1f11647e","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:49:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_8be18b33b8654d1aac5cfc1bee291acb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1237b87b10953e38c7cb8aab718dcc62c645bbd626c91b2ae6bf8ea340c4a33f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A CLI batch mode exists via `paperbanana run` with parameters including `--task_name` (diagram/plot), `--exp_mode`, `--provider`, `--max_critic_rounds`, `--retrieval_setting`, and `--resume`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1561d16e3c18bdfa2a4e070c416a37d8e71cd3c1c116ca66ad29d27714773882"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Generation runs as background async jobs with a real-time event timeline, supporting 40+ concurrent candidates, and results are packaged in a `Bundle v1` `.bundle.json` format preserving timelines and review records."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3a201638417ed92d8adc18ed4a376bafe0763cbeebf626a1a947b0ab287344fb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes a registry-driven pipeline (Pipeline Registry) intended to replace hardcoded branching so new flows can be added via configuration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5588a8342f3ace10314a02d4cebd747ff1937202b4528caa37e4fd5e7f8876df"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A refinement workspace supports 2K/4K upscaling with concurrent multi-version redraws, tree-shaped version chains, and rollback to any historical version."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a466f19b3198a1faef61d08b80bd5b16594978d7455e4387f93f708b6d2af9dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented pipeline comprises six stages: Retriever (few-shot retrieval), Planner (structured visual descriptions), Stylist, Visualizer (image or Matplotlib code), Critic (multi-round review), and optional Polish."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ac03c62e4edd93b3f87de8f7adbb13defc4dbcadc0059ee6f5fd6bbc7d9ba421"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states Google has patented the original PaperBanana multi-agent pipeline methodology, so the pipeline logic must not be used commercially, a restriction that also applies to PaperBanana-Pro."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c5d4dcb7b586f28bac7bfe1d42d60acdf54d61e75267bedc718a63e234ba6942"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The optional PaperBananaBench dataset (dwzhu/PaperBananaBench on Hugging Face) supplies few-shot reference examples and an evaluation benchmark; retrieval can be set to `none` to skip it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e0bc7f42fde1e400631e8ccbd4af452b56b3082bc6269ef5a45363d645f48a89"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project targets Python 3.12 or later, installs via `uv sync --locked` plus `uv tool install --editable .`, and requirements.txt contains an editable self-dependency."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f3f3f6931e228ef502bad0b250cdb3cbdc3f47c8b06d880259acdfc7db7d5b8e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Four providers are officially supported: Gemini, OpenAI, Openrouter, and Evolink; any OpenAI-compatible API can also be added by supplying a Base URL."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f770a7da148a22dc7c290bd622544031dc09e63d261359e243ba1b971b87fe73"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a `paperbanana` command whose default form launches a GUI frontend on port 8501, equivalent to `paperbanana gui`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f835d5bb76b505be2e094af333cd641ffe2b0b689e8862a47e15a80d8d82a959"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A viewer subcommand offers `paperbanana viewer evolution` for pipeline evolution and `paperbanana viewer eval` for evaluation-with-reference review."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1237b87b10953e38c7cb8aab718dcc62c645bbd626c91b2ae6bf8ea340c4a33f","clm_1561d16e3c18bdfa2a4e070c416a37d8e71cd3c1c116ca66ad29d27714773882","clm_3a201638417ed92d8adc18ed4a376bafe0763cbeebf626a1a947b0ab287344fb","clm_5588a8342f3ace10314a02d4cebd747ff1937202b4528caa37e4fd5e7f8876df","clm_a466f19b3198a1faef61d08b80bd5b16594978d7455e4387f93f708b6d2af9dc","clm_ac03c62e4edd93b3f87de8f7adbb13defc4dbcadc0059ee6f5fd6bbc7d9ba421","clm_c5d4dcb7b586f28bac7bfe1d42d60acdf54d61e75267bedc718a63e234ba6942","clm_e0bc7f42fde1e400631e8ccbd4af452b56b3082bc6269ef5a45363d645f48a89","clm_f3f3f6931e228ef502bad0b250cdb3cbdc3f47c8b06d880259acdfc7db7d5b8e","clm_f770a7da148a22dc7c290bd622544031dc09e63d261359e